  "answers": [
    {
      "questionId": "q0",
      "value": "q0_pay_when_roi_clear",
      "rationale": "As a busy parent juggling multiple responsibilities, I'd want to see concrete evidence that FocusLoop actually reduces my stress and saves time before committing to a subscription. The free tier lets me validate the ROI first.",
      "confidence": 0.88
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q1",
      "value": "q1_plus_after_sustained_use",
      "rationale": "Once I'm confident the app is working for my household, Plus makes sense for the digest and handoffs. Pro's email parsing is nice but not essential enough to jump to immediately—I'd upgrade to Plus first and see if the extra $5 for Pro becomes necessary.",
      "confidence": 0.82
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q2",
      "value": "q2_monthly_cancel_anytime",
      "rationale": "I prefer flexibility as a parent—life changes, priorities shift, and I don't want to be locked into annual prepay. Monthly lets me cancel guilt-free if the app stops fitting our needs.",
      "confidence": 0.85
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q3",
      "value": "q3_one_dollar_try_cancel",
      "rationale": "A $1 first month is a low-friction way to test Plus features in a real household context. I'd use it seriously for a month and cancel unless the digest and handoffs genuinely simplify our coordination.",
      "confidence": 0.87
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q4",
      "value": "q4_compare_pay_if_wins",
      "rationale": "I'm not dogmatic about free vs. paid, but I also won't waste time hunting for alternatives. If a friend recommends a paid app, I'd compare it fairly to what I'm using—and pay only if it clearly wins on the metrics that matter (ease, reliability, family buy-in).",
      "confidence": 0.83
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q5",
      "value": "q5_ads_pay_if_plus_useful",
      "rationale": "Ads on the free tier are tolerable, but they're not the reason I'd upgrade. I'd pay for Plus because of the digest and handoffs—ad-free is a bonus, not the driver.",
      "confidence": 0.84
    },
    {
      "questionId": "q6",
      "value": "q6_fair_if_use_justifies",
      "rationale": "At $6.99/month for Plus, the pricing is reasonable if daily use justifies it. For a tool that genuinely reduces household chaos and missed deadlines, that's fair value. But it only works if adoption sticks.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "questionId": "overall_interest",
      "value": 4,
      "rationale": "FocusLoop directly solves a real pain point—fragmented coordination across WeChat, email, and paper. As a dual-income parent with school-age kids, this resonates strongly. Not a 5 because success depends on whether my whole family actually uses it.",
      "confidence": 0.86
    },
    {
      "questionId": "would_try_beta",
      "value": "true",
      "rationale": "Absolutely. The problem is urgent enough that I'd want early access to shape the product. Beta users often get better support and can influence features—that's worth the risk of rough edges.",
      "confidence": 0.89
    }
  ],
